"""How many AI requests run at once, and how many lines feed them.

Two settings decide AI throughput:

* ``ai_concurrency`` – requests allowed in flight at the same time;
* the lines one request carries – ``ai_scene_batch_size`` in Scene mode,
  ``ai_batch_size`` in JSON/XML mode, at most 50 for Gemini.

Before this module the pipeline handed the engine one request's worth of
lines per step, so Scene/JSON/XML always ran a single request whatever
``ai_concurrency`` said, and OpenAI/Gemini used fixed semaphores (5 and 3).
Now a pipeline step holds one request per parallel slot and every engine's
semaphore follows the setting, within the provider's own ceiling.

Requests keep the same lines in the same order; only how many are sent side
by side changes. The project work queue stays serial.
"""
pass
from typing import Any as LN_src_core_ai_parallel__Any, Optional as LN_src_core_ai_parallel__Optional
