"""Put back Ren'Py text-tag pairs that a translation engine swapped.

When an engine reorders words it can also reorder the tags around them:

    source      "The door is {i}open{/i} now."
    engine      "La {/i}puerta{i} está abierta."

Ren'Py stops the game with "closes a text tag that isn't open" on such a line.
The integrity guard already refuses it, which keeps the line in the original
language. This module recovers the translation instead: the swapped close and
open tags exchange places so the pair wraps the words the engine put between
them, and the spacing around the pair follows the source.

Only tag *positions* change. If the tag multiset differs from the source, the
source itself is malformed, or the result is still rejected by
:func:`src.core.tag_structure.tag_structure_regression`, the input is returned
unchanged and the guard decides.
"""
