"""Save-safe Ren'Py translation output.

Ren'Py saves point at statement names, and Ren'Py keeps those names stable
across recompiles by reading the previous ``.rpyc``. Moving a ``translate``
block to another file, renaming a file or deleting its ``.rpyc`` gives every
statement a new name, and loading an older save then fails with "Couldn't find
a place to stop rolling back". The rules here follow from that:

* Dialogue blocks (``translate <lang> <id>:``) stay in the file that already
  holds them; new ones go to the base file, named after the source script.
* ``translate <lang> strings`` pairs carry no statement names. They fill a file
  up to ``max_strings_bytes``; only the overflow goes to ``__ln_partNNN``
  files. This keeps very large files from exhausting Ren'Py 7's memory while it
  compiles them (MemoryError seen with Photo Hunt on Ren'Py 7.4.4).
* ``.rpyc`` files are never deleted, except the one of a strings-only file this
  writer itself removes, which Ren'Py would otherwise still load.
* Files LinguaNova did not write are never rewritten; their keys are only read
  so nothing is duplicated.
* Layouts written by earlier versions keep their file names.

Backups of every rewritten file live outside ``game/``, where Ren'Py cannot
load them.
"""
