    '- Choosing a game starts a whole-game analysis (`.rpy`, `.rpyc` and `.rpa`) kept in\n'
    '  memory for the session only. Its character names are kept untranslated in every run;\n'
    '  the extractor button adds them and recurring proper nouns to the current glossary.\n'
    '- Empty translations are pending terms: kept in the file, never applied.\n'
    '- The glossary page header names the game and language being edited.\n'
    '\n'
    '### 54. The MOD completes an existing translation instead of adding a second language — 2026-11-05\n'
    '\n'
    '- The interface MOD completes the language the game already has, whatever it is called:\n'
    '  it matches game/tl/ folders by folder name, by the name declared in\n'
    '  `translate <language>` (catalogue aliases, accents ignored: espanol, Español,\n'
    '  castellano...) or, failing both, by detecting the language of the folder\'s\n'
    '  translated text. It registers its strings under that same Ren\'Py language, so\n'
    '  the player sees one language, never a second "Spanish".\n'
    '- The MOD\'s own data files are looked up first in that exact folder (manual\n'
    '  corrections included).\n'
    '- Share package: when the translation in a folder was made by someone else and\n'
    '  LinguaNova only added MOD data there, only LinguaNova\'s files are packed.\n'
    '\n'
    '### 55. The MOD never touches game/tl/ and joins the game\'s own language — 2026-11-05\n'
    '\n'
    '- Fixed rule: the MOD never writes into game/tl/ (no edits, no extra files), whoever\n'
    '  made the translations there. Its data lives in game/zz_linguanova/mod/<language>/;\n'
    '  data left in game/tl/<language>/ by earlier versions is moved there, and a tl/\n'
    '  folder the MOD itself had created is removed once empty.\n'
    '- When the game starts, if it has (now or after a future update) a language with the\n'
    '  same or a similar name that holds its own translation, the MOD fills THAT language\n'
    '  and hides its own from the menu; a player who had chosen the MOD\'s language is moved\n'
    '  to the game\'s. No regeneration is needed.\n'
